      "citations": [
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00342",
          "explanation": "Doctor explicitly closes the episode without pretending to settle lifetime neurodevelopmental risk, acknowledging that prior severe asphyxia/HIE history warrants follow-up even when today's home state is reassuring.",
          "quote": "我帮你整理成这几天的极简清单"
        },
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00128",
          "explanation": "Doctor explains that the baby's prior severe history (asphyxia, HIE, infection) requires planned follow-up despite current stability, embodying safe bounded closure that carries residual risk forward.",
          "quote": "宝宝出生后因为窒息、脑病、感染住院，刚出院没几天"
        }
      ],
      "completion": "complete",
      "explanation": "The doctor consistently frames the plan around the fact that the baby's current stable state is reassuring for today but does not erase the serious perinatal history; follow-up is explicitly scheduled for neurodevelopmental and haematologic monitoring, and the caregiver is told to bring the discharge summary and medicines to the clinic. This directly satisfies the HO4 description of closing the current result-return episode while acknowledging that prior severe asphyxia/HIE warrants scheduled follow-up without pretending to settle lifetime risk.",
      "ho_id": "HO4",
      "meaningful_trajectory_impact": true,
      "triggered": true
    }
  ],
